cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite as below."
type: software
title: "TR-FactBench: A Multi-Domain Benchmark for Source-Grounded Factuality Verification in Turkish"
authors:
  - family-names: "Dalga"
    given-names: "Engin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EngindalgaMaku/tr-factbench"
url: "https://github.com/EngindalgaMaku/tr-factbench"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0-preview"
date-released: "2026-07-30"
abstract: >
  TR-FactBench is a 4-class source-grounded factuality verification benchmark
  for Turkish. It covers three domains (finance, legal, medical) with 4,800
  training, 960 general dev, and 600 stress-test examples. The benchmark
  evaluates fine-tuned Turkish encoder models (including ELECTRA and ModernBERT)
  and four zero-shot/few-shot LLM baselines.

keywords:
  - Turkish NLP
  - factuality verification
  - hallucination detection
  - natural language inference
  - LoRA
  - ELECTRA

note: >
  Research preview. The first independent blind-human pass is complete for both
  evaluation sets (DEV960 960/960; Dev600 600/600). Single-annotator provisional
  evaluation files are included. Second annotation and adjudication are reserved
  for a later stable release; do not treat this preview as fully adjudicated gold.